# Editor and tool state: per-machine, never shared. settings.local.json is the
# one that kept getting committed.
.claude/*
.vs/
.DS_Store

# Skills are the exception: they are project tooling, written once and useful to
# everyone working here, so they belong in the repo rather than on one machine.
!.claude/skills/

# Debug profiles carry local paths, so they stay out for every project rather
# than being listed one project at a time.
launchSettings.json

# Site build output. client/, server/ and site/ each have their own .gitignore
# for the rest; these two are the roots nothing else claims.
.svelte-kit/
.vite/

# Scratch output: corpus sweep reports and anything else a local run produces.
#
# A whole folder rather than a list of filenames, because the point is that
# NOTHING written here is committable. Their contents are a snapshot of whichever
# game installs happen to be on one machine, so committing one would be
# committing somebody's local state — and a filename pattern only protects the
# names somebody thought of.
/temp/

# The same reports if they are written anywhere else, since GSCODE_SWEEP_REPORT
# can point at any directory.
gscode-sweep-*.html
